= <span style="color: #CC0000;">**UDF**</span> and <span style="color: #1FA6D6;">**BDR**</span> Alliance

With the splitting of the <span style="color: #CC0000;">**UDF**</span>'s Left wing, the party is in decline once again.

The <span style="color: #CC0000;">**UDF**</span>, desperate for a way out, has reached a deal with FlowBerryFizzler of the <span style="color: #1FA6D6;">**BDR**</span>

Time will tell what this means for the Social Democratic party.

- @dvp_left_split

@dvp_left_split
title: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s left wing splits!
on-arrival: hugenberg_dvp = 1; old_middle_dvp *= 0.8; new_middle_dvp *= 0.5; catholics_dvp *= 0.8; pro_republic -= 3; liberal_cooperation -= 10; bourgeois_cooperation -= 10; dvp_right += 25; dvp_relation -= 50
face-image: img/dvp_poster_2.jpg

Those on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s left wing who had quietly opposed Dingeldey's turn to the right have now resigned en masse. Hans Bechly, Frank Glatzel, and Otto Thiel—prominent figures within the white-collar DHV union—have also stepped down, with Bechly being the longtime chairman of the association.

With their exodus, the party’s last remaining link to the German white-collar movement has been severed, along with a significant portion of its electoral base. The only consolation Dingeldey can claim is that the party’s loss in seats will be somewhat mitigated by its electoral connection to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>.
